# Range Proof — "I know x such that x is in [lo, hi] and H(x) == y"
#
# Proves a secret value falls within a public range without
# revealing the value itself. The hash binds the secret to a
# public commitment so the same proof can't be reused.
#
# This demonstrates: secret inputs, public inputs, comparisons, hashing.

Secret Int Inputs: (x)
Public Int Inputs: (lo, hi, y)

compute: h = H(x)
check: y == h
check: x >= lo
check: x <= hi
